        "Tsvi Segal",
        "Ya'akov Yisrael Levenshtam",
        "Yosef b. Zalman Schnur" ;
    gndo:language "Hebrew" ;
    gndo:owner "Bodleian Library, Oxford",
        "Columbia University Libraries",
        "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library",
        "National Library of Israel",
        "The Library of the Katz Center for Advanced Judaic Studies" ;
    gndo:printer "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/590d82f1-9b0b-5990-a28d-eaddf7d8b1f7",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/c44e9334-95f5-57a2-9210-fc9e3dfbb110" ;
    jl:describedAt "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000153142&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000153143&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000153144&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "",
        "All notes by Chaim Meiselman:   notes    Title taken from Song of Songs 1-13: sachet of myrrh.      Double column scheme of print, headed only by the weekly portion being expounded (’Sidrah’). Block script.      This literary work is one combining homiletics, Biblical interpretations, and commentary on the Zohar for the weekly Torah portions.      The exact date of printing is contradictory between the title information and that on the colophon. The title reads ’Shevat 327’, i.e. Feb. 1567, while the colophon reads ’ ... today, sixth day (Friday), 5326 (1566)’ while not stating which month this is being written in.      The leaves at the end of the volume skip paginations. This is noted by Steinschneider (op.cit.) ’ ed. castrata ’ .      Printers device on title, featuring an elephant carrying a warring legion in Hellenic dress. Two Hellenic figures grace the sides - possibly Aphrodite and Adonis. A bust of a man centers the bottom, wearing contemporary headwear. Engraved above: Tarde Set Tuto (Late, but safe).      Architechtural title illustration. Flora adorns two wavy columns, headed by double urns.   references    Benjakob, Otsar Hasefarim, 212 : 4th entry      Friedberg, Beit Eked Sefarim, tsadi 431 : 3      Steinschneider, Cat. Libr. Bodl., 4301 : 3.",
        "date given on title page as shin-vav month of Tishre printers colophon gives day of week (Friday) but fails to note month or day of month." ;
    dc:publisher "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/63925f45-10a8-54da-a4ed-023f8a4bbba5" ;
    dc:title "Tseror Ha-mor" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-18T02:08:16.989108"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Tseror Ha-mor" .

