        "https://search.worldcat.org/de/title/122919928" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "",
        "Notes by Chaim Meiselman.  Block Hebrew text (of Prayer) surrounded on the outsidess by a Yiddish elucidation. Over each column of Yiddish, the Hebrew catch-word connects the elucidation and the prayers; this scheme begins each paragraph of the elucidation, but these catch-words aren’t in bold block.      Title ornament scheme has three clusters topping a frame, with an extra row of flora and two bottom-triangles on the bottom. Seal of the city of Dyherrnfurth (’Sigilium Civitatis Duhrenfurtensis’) crowned around St. George killing a dragon, the traditional coat-of-arms to Dyhernfurth.   references    Bibliography of the Hebrew Book, no. 000182769" ;
    dc:publisher "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/8947c8cc-28fa-5def-8b24-027a351d7a0f",
