    gndo:printer "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/807213c1-e217-54ed-90d1-2f35256728cc" ;
    jl:describedAt "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000110734&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000110741&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://search.worldcat.org/de/title/762415209" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "Notes by Chaim Meiselman:   Very rare edition. Many of the printing-plates were pressed off center, making the print seem more crude. Ink-blotches (likely from a loose plate). Printed double colums, with running title.  הובא לדפוס במצות כבוד רב האי גאון החסיד האלוקי המפורסם ... מוה לוי יצחק אבד דקק בארדיטשוב. Transl.: Brought to press at the command of his honor, that ga'on, the pious and Godly, the famous Rabbi Levi Yitsḥak, Av-Beth-Din of the Holy Community of Barditshev (Berdychiv - Ukraine). Levi Yitsḥak of Barditshev, ca. 1740-1809, was a famous Hassidic personality and early student of Dov-Baer (ha-Maggid) of Mezeritch. His involvement with the printing of 'Rishonim' such as this title is less well-known.  Freidberg, Ch. B. Bet Eked Sepharim,vol. 3, 260 (6).Ben-Jakob, Otsar ha-Sefarim, 261." ;
    dc:publisher "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/f95ca40c-10c7-5d56-b329-85765662e4cd" ;
    dc:title "Rokeah" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-17T20:55:58.863477"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rokeah" .

