        "Russian State Library",
        "The Library of the Katz Center for Advanced Judaic Studies" ;
    gndo:printer "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/63925f45-10a8-54da-a4ed-023f8a4bbba5" ;
    jl:describedAt "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000333273&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000334101&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000334234&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000334430&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,122710726&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://search.worldcat.org/de/title/122856046" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "",
        "Note that on the title page of the first printed edition of Bomberg's Masekhet Horayot it states that there were no Tosafot that they could find commenting on this tractate and so they added the Jerusalem Talmud to the volume despite the fact that they had not done that in other volumes printed prior to this one. Also note that most printed editions of Horayot are corrupt and that Bomberg's 1521 edition is considered the best text.  Ehrman, Arnost Zvi. Horayot. Encyclopaedia Judaica, edited by Michael Berenbaum and Fred Skolnik, 2nd ed., vol. 9, Macmillan Reference USA, 2007, p. 524. Gale Virtual Reference Library, go.galegroup.com/ps/i.do?p=GVRL&sw=w&u=nysl_me_jethsoa&v=2.1&id=GALE%7CCX2587509188&it=r&asid=869eeadc64be21cb7e58662912aedf0e. Accessed 27 June 2017.",
        "The format of the page is different than for other tractates. The Gemara text is on one side and the commentary on the other. You do not have Gemara text surrounded by commentary. I am assuming that is because Bomberg, as he notes on the title page, that he found no Tosafot associated with this tractate. He also added the Yerushalmi to the end of the tractate something he notes that he did NOT do on other tractates (although I think Shekalim has Yerushalmi)." ;
    dc:publisher "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/0f050232-597e-5c73-871e-02c318253a27",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/63925f45-10a8-54da-a4ed-023f8a4bbba5",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/7e7793ae-9ab9-57b8-bc9e-dd50abe94e5f" ;
    dc:title "Talmud. Horayot" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-18T00:55:40.473476"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Talmud. Horayot" .

<http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/204d2ff9-82d6-549a-81eb-e7a9c8238b8e> a gndo:Work ;
    gndo:associatedPlace "Frankfurta which is on a desert",
        "Shkroŭ",
        "Škloŭ",
        "פרנקפורטיאה אשר על אודרה" ;
    gndo:author "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/0c888d5c-de27-5c83-9477-6f68903c57ed",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/44696231-288d-5264-8e69-c5c9ba3aa839" ;
    gndo:dateOfPublication "1691 - 1692",
        "1812 - 1814" ;
    gndo:dedicatee "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/2a992c6c-ff82-5b77-9ae9-317a3eae1bc9" ;
    gndo:formerOwner "Archbishop Marsh's Library",
        "Baltimore Hebrew College",
        "Beit ha-Midrash Aryeh-Leyb ben Eli'ezer, Vilna",
        "Isaac Katz",
        "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library" ;
    gndo:language "Aramaic",
        "Hebrew" ;
    gndo:owner "Archbishop Marsh's Library",
        "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library" ;
    gndo:printer "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/13a72317-d50b-517d-a140-3286cb7f48b4" ;
    jl:describedAt "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000146437&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,001987369&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "Notes by Chaim Meiselman:   Chronograms from each volume: Vol. 1 - ‫ ל’ך אני הו’שיעני כ’י’ פק’ו’דיך דרשת’י [תקעב]. ‬Vol. 2 - שמות, [ויקרא]. לך אני הוש’יעני כי פקוד’יך דר’שתי [תקעד].  Haskamah on the edition from Yisrael-Leyb Mirkes of Minsk, Mosheh b. Yisra'el of Kopys, Tsvi-Hirsh b. Ya'akov of Smolyany, dated Friday 6 Adar, 1812.  Full folio of diagrams depicting the Midrashic arguments of the measurements and shapes of Noah's ark; Vol. 1, folio no. 35.  Blue-gray paper; honorary device on the center of the title for Alexander I. An ark, with two chalices surrounding the apex and large urns to each side, models AP (Aleksandr Pavlovich) with a crown above. A bird rests on the apex.  Similar folio editions of the Midrash with commentaries were created in the Pale-of-Settlement area during the turn of the 18th-19th centuries; Mynkivtsi (1799), Ostrog (1805), Zolkiew (1808), Lemberg (1808), Mogilev (1809), Berdichyv (1811), Sudylkiv (1820), among others. These were typeset in the form created for the folio Midrash editions in Germany, 1700-1750 ca., in which many of the commentaries surrounding the text were printed for the first time.  Friedberg, Beit Eked Sefarim,mem 783 : 27" ;
    dc:contributor "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/83361272-3658-5ab6-a1d3-fff0ae42a28c",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/b6f2eb6b-7232-5836-959b-e57e6a9e23ed",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/c259eae2-aea5-59b9-b897-ca9305a9498c" ;
    dc:publisher "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/50463d8d-4e33-51fa-a052-ac24114f49d3" ;
    dc:title "Midrash Rabbah. Pentateuch. Five Scrolls. Commentary" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-17T18:29:16.275762"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Midrash Rabbah. Pentateuch. Five Scrolls. Commentary" .

