    jl:hasAbstract "All notes and transcriptions by Chaim Meiselman:  The Christian synagogue :wherein is contained the diverse reading, the right poynting, translation, and collation of Scripture with Scripture : with the customes of the Hebrewes and proselytes, and of all those nations, with whom they were conversant | digested into three bookes ... : serving generally for a helpe to the vnderstanding of all ... but more specially for all young students in divinitie ... /by Iohn Weemse.  The 2nd ed., corrected, and amended.London :Printed by I.D. for Iohn Bellamie ...,1623.[18], 308 p. :2 ill. ;21 cm. (4to)Signatures:)(⁴ A⁴ B-2R⁴( -2R₄ blank).Head pieces, tail piece, initials.STC (2nd ed.)25210a.5.This is the second and revised edition of The Christian Synagogue by John Weemse (s.v. Wemyss or Weemes), a minister in the Church of Scotland. The volume is missionizing in nature with specific focus on the Jews attempting the cohorting of Jews and Jewish Tradition via the missionizing mission of the Church.Contents of the volume range from quotes of Scripture, Old and New Testaments, and sayings from Talmudic sages. Paragraphs scattered in the volume also cite historical sources in regard to the History of the Jews.1: Prolegomena 2: Of the Canonical and Apocryphe Bookes 3: Of the externall meanes. Second Booke: 1: of the Sense of the Scriptures 2: on the Illustration of Doctrine. Possibly an afterword: on the Blessing of the people.McAlpin Coll.,I, p. 353.(from t.p.) The first, shewing the meanes both inward and outward, to attaine to the knowledge of the sense of the whole Scriptures --The second, unfolding the true sense of the Scripture it selfe ... -- The third, teaching the true manner of confirmation, illustration, and application of doctrines, rightly gathered from the true sense of Scripture.With an introduction by the author to Thomas, first Earl of Melrose; undated, signed I. W. of Lathoquar." ;
    dc:title "The Christian synagogue" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-18T01:31:23.132982"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "The Christian synagogue" .

