    jl:hasAbstract "",
        "Berlin and Frankfurt on der Oder",
        "Note that this edition of the Talmud was a shared project of two cities--Berlin and Frankfurt de Oder. The printer was Aaron ben Moshe Rofe, but he was backed by Jablonski and Grillo of Frankfurt de Oder.  See http://www.jewishvirtuallibrary.org/hebrew-printing  Title page of this imprint says in latin— Opus in quo de Benedictionibus de gratis DEO agendis De Orationibus and Divinis Laudibus agitur Recognitum a Marco Marino Brix. Can. Regul D. Servatoris Er ab omnibus iis quae contra Religionem Chriftianan funt Juxta mentem Concilii Tredentini expurgatum Ade ut non modo citra Impietatem, verum etiam cum frictu legi poffit Prout jam ante hac Cum Privilegio SACR. CAESAR MAJ. And Sereniffimorum Regem POLG And PRVSSIAE Fis emiffum fuit Denuo editum Berolini and Francofvrti",
        "Subtitle: (... עם פירוש רשי ותוספו' ופסקיהן והמשניות עם באור הרמבם זל והמרדכי גדול).<br />BHB note: אוצר 26 A" ;
    dc:publisher "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/0f050232-597e-5c73-871e-02c318253a27",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/1818b22e-b8e3-5e80-9b23-9362f19dacde",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/768cca8f-c2c8-51fc-baac-a17bfecdab93" ;
    dc:title "Talmud. Berakhot" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-18T00:51:11.647502"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Talmud. Berakhot" .

