    jl:hasAbstract "",
        "115 p. 22 cm.",
        "8 leaves. 2nd edition.",
        "91 p. 19 cm.",
        "<p>It appears it was published sometime between the first of Tishrei in 5493, or September 20th, 1732 through the 29th of Elul, or September 9th, 1733. https://huc.on.worldcat.org/oclc/122771470</p>",
        "All notes by Chaim Meiselman:  Text in Hebrew, with a portion in Yiddish (f. 8 verso). There are two title pages, the first with the title Seder sheḥiṭot u-vediḳot and the second with the title Seder bediḳot. The first part is about the inspection of the slaughtering knife and the laws of kosher slaughter, and the second is about the inspection of the animal for imperfections which would render it unkosher (such as imperfections in the lungs and heart chambers. Titles within an architectural border. The printers device of Uri ben Aaron ha-Levi is on the verso of each title page (two fish, and a pitcher pouring water) and a final on the last page. Also found on the upper framing of the title pages. Title acknowledges the reigning monarch, Augustus II the Strong (1670-1733), referring to him as Friedrich Augustus. Text of the halakhic code of R. Jacob Weill is in the upper center of each page in square print, with his commentary surrounding it in smaller print. Signatures: [1-6]⁴.  Not in the Bibliography of the Hebrew Book. Vinograd, Zolkiew 20 Title indicates that the editors of the volume were descendants (or relatives) of the printer, Shelomoh b. Mosheh Ṿelḥ (ועלח, or Wolch) and Aharon b. Daṿid ha-Levi.  Illustrations on f. 5 verso are of slaughter knife blades, showing a kosher knife and three types of imperfections on knives. Also shown on f. 16 recto are openings of the Bronchial Tree, using a bold square samekh (ס) turned sidewards.",
        "All notes by Chaim Meiselman:  Two title pages, the first featuring Sheḥiṭot u-vediḳot and the second featuring Bediḳot. Title pages are within architechtural schemes and decorated columns. Illustrations are mixed with the text. A depiction of the bronchial opening on folio 12 recto, lung adhesions on folio 13 verso, and polyps on the lung walls on 14 recto. With a quick manual for slaughter called Derekh ha-sheḥiṭah bi-ḳetsarah on the title page verso. The text of R. Jacob Weill's code is printed in square type on the insides of the folios, and his notes (assembled by Tsevi Hirsch b. Yitsḥaḳ Yaʿaḳov of Kraków) are printed in small type at the outside of the columns. Signatures: 1-[8]² 9² (-9[-2]).",
        "Approbation letters by Moses Minz, Moses Deutsch, Moses Schreiber and others. Laws concerning slaughtering of animals,w ith a large commentary by Isaac Munkacs",
        "BHB note: הטופס שלפנינו פגום. חסרים השער והדף האחרון ונותרו ששה דפים בלבד. כנראה היו בטופס השלם שמונה דפים.",
        "Imperfect: title page partially torn and repaired affecting text. Autographs of Samuel Lubsehinsko; Semaik(?) Samuel; A. Wernberg.",
        "Includes inscriptions. Library's copy lacks title page and leaves. Library's copy has 27 unnumbered, handwritten pages.",
        "It appears it was printed sometime in 5505, or 1744-1745, between the first of Tishrei, on September 7, 1744 , the 29th of Elul, September 26, 1745. https://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%94%27%D7%AA%D7%A7%22%D7%94",
        "It appears this was published sometime between the first of Tishrei, 5483, or September 12th, 1722 to the 29th of Elul, 5483, or September 29th, 1723.  https://huc.on.worldcat.org/search?sortKey=BEST_MATCH&databaseList=638&queryString=kw%3A%28Shehitot+u-vedikot%29+AND+au%3A%28Weil%2C+Jacob%29&changedFacet=year&overrideStickyFacetDefault=&selectSortKey=BEST_MATCH&clusterResults=on&expandSearch=on&overrideGroupVariant=&overrideGroupVariantValue=&scope=wz%3A17&format=all&year=custom&yearFrom=1600&yearTo=1800&author=all&topic=all&database=all&language=all&materialtype=all#/oclc/122713174",
        "It says Lvov, Tiknu, 1776. So we know it was published sometime in the Hebrew calendar year of 5556. Wikipedia says: Tiknu, meaning short remedial justice, is a Hebrew year that began on the first of Tishrei, or September 14, 1795, and ended on the 29th of Elul, or October 2, 1796. https://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%94%27%D7%AA%D7%A7%D7%A0%22%D7%95",
        "Subtitle: [עם פירוש זבח טוב מאת ר' יהודה ליברמן בר יוסף].<br />BHB note: הוצאה מאוחרת: פראג תז.",
        "Subtitle: מסקינן דשחיטה מן הצואר... [מאת] (מהרי ווייל זל).<br />BHB note: קולופון: נדפס פה קק פראג... השחיטות והבדיקות, על ידי ... משה בר גרשם הכהן מחקק.",
        "There is a hand-written inscription which says Eisenberg on one of the cover pages, so it appears someone named Eisenberg once owned this copy." ;
