<http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/3d212105-9f5c-5fef-acde-26656f458bac> a gndo:Work ;
    gndo:associatedPlace "Fiorda",
        "פיורדא" ;
    gndo:author "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/48b93270-62df-5352-95a7-3f1b1a62ee78" ;
    gndo:dateOfPublication "1798" ;
    gndo:formerOwner "Baltimore Hebrew College",
        "Isaac Gündersheim",
        "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library" ;
    gndo:language "Hebrew" ;
    gndo:owner "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library" ;
    gndo:printer "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/3d4edbb5-a70a-5b24-9721-65b8bcf387d0" ;
    jl:describedAt "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,001196408&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "Notes by Chaim Meiselman  First and only printing.Author statement on title: המחבר... מאיר בלאא כהרר זלמן שיף כץ זללהה אשר... נתעלה להיות ראשון בבהמד ההוקם על יד... כה ליב בן... רא [אליהו] רייס זל, וראש בד בקק פפורט [פרנקפורט] דמיין... Transl: the author Meir son of Zalman Shif, who rose to head the academy begun by Leib son of R.A. (Eliyahu) Reiss, and (Shif) is the Head of Beth-Din in Frankfurt Am-Main. Chronogram: לפרט ו'ל'ב'ב'י' ר'ח'ש' דבר טוב. Steinschneider, Catalogus Libris Hebraeorum,6326:1. Ben-Jakob, Otsar HaSefarim,daled 403. Friedberg, Beit Eked Sefarim,daled 1114.Derekh Aniyah, trans. Voyage of the Ship, is the title of the work, taken from Proverbs 30:19. The way of an eagle in the air; the way of a serpent on a rock; , and the way of a man with a maid.. Common practice of Rabbinic writing is to not write y. and h. together, and to replace y. with an elipsis - hence the title statement Derekh Aniy' .  The author's name, Shif, is probably the meaning of his naming the volume Way of the Ship. Printed in double columns." ;
    dc:title "Derekh Aniyah" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-17T14:39:33.258477"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Derekh Aniyah" .

