        "https://search.worldcat.org/de/title/233345270" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "",
        "<p>A SCARCE, MINIATURE GEMARA. &ldquo;This enigmatic pocket edition of Tractate Sukah fits comfortably into the palm of a hand. It is the smallest recorded printed talmudic tractate. It does not include any commentaries, an indication that this edition was printed under the influence of the Maharal of Prague&rdquo; - who emphasized the fundamental importance of regularly reviewing one&rsquo;s studies; mastering the text, before proceeding to a more advanced focus on the commentaries.</p>",
        "<p>Bomberg</p>" ;
