    jl:hasAbstract "Notes by Chaim Meiselman :  General Note  Edited by Vittorio Oliano, grandson of the great grammarian, Elijah Bahur Sega'L.  General Note  Printers device on title, featuring an elephant carrying a warring legion in Hellenic dress. Two Hellenic figures grace the sides - possibly Aphrodite and Adonis. A bust of a man centers the bottom, in contemporary headwear. Engraved above: Tarde Set Tuto (Late, but safe).  Citation/Ref. Note    Steinschneider, Cat.Lib.Bodl., 5302:39.  General Note  Originally published: Venice, 1544 or 1545.  General Note  Translations of the author's Sirāj.  General Note  With a poem by León Hebreo (Judah Abravanel)" ;
    dc:title "Naḥalat Avot" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-17T20:00:48.043309"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Naḥalat Avot" .

