    jl:describedAt "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000135022&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "Also known as: Catechismus hebraice      Also known as: Rudimenta fidei Christianae hebraicis literis      Ḥinukh beḥire Yah   notes    Translation by Immanuel Tremellius of Jean Calvin’s Catéchisme de l’Eglise de Genève.      Alternate titles from: Calvin, J. Opera quae supersunt omnia (i.e. Works. 1863), vols. LVIII-LIX. Catalogus operum Calvini chronologicus, column 472; and Index Aureliensis.      Date layout: 1-8-20 (א’ תתך) to Our Lord, 580 (תקפ’) to the count of the Jews. Taken from imprint.   language    Primarily in Hebrew; Epistola dedicatoria (p. [3]-9; a letter from Tremellius to Duke Christoph of Württemberg, dated April 3, 1554, in Strasbourg) in Latin." ;
    dc:title "Catéchisme de l'Eglise de Genève.Hebrew" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-17T14:31:51.771443"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Catéchisme de l'Eglise de Genève.Hebrew" .

