    gndo:language "German",
        "Greek",
        "Hebrew",
        "Latin" ;
    gndo:owner "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library" ;
    gndo:printer "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/a6f58075-36fc-5066-9adf-2b42551d3991" ;
    jl:describedAt "https://search.worldcat.org/de/title/603686288" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "<p>All notes by Chaim Meiselman. Double-columns, sometimes separated by a printer&rsquo;s ruling; Errata, glossary, and index at the end. Printers device at the end of Hebrew index. Each plate of illustration is numbered to illustrate a passage in the text. Index of folio-sized illustrations: Gr&uuml;nd-muss der Stifts-h&uuml;tter (the Tabernacle) ; die Wohnung der Stiffts-h&uuml;tte (upper view of the Tabernacle) ; ibid. ; Das Heilige (The Holies) ; Das Allerheiligiste (Holy-of-Holies) ; die Bundeslade mit der Besten-seuse (the Ark of the Covenant and the Incense-burning) ; B&uuml;ldner Leuchter (mit. 3 brennenden / mit. 7 brenennden (Extra-Candelabra, with 3 burning / 7 burning) ; Schau-Brod Tisch - mit den Spregeln ohne die Schau-Brod / mit den Schau-Brod (Show-Bread table with the slats empty of Show-Brad / With the Show-Bread) - pullout engraving ; Der R&auml;usch-Altar so im heiligen gestander / Das Eherne hand-wass (The Iron Hand-Wash) ; des Brandopfers-Altars in der Stiffts-H&uuml;tter (the Fire-Altar of the Tabernacle) ; Addenda - (Seals of the Kingship of Jerusalem in Ivri and Ashuri - Palaeo-Hebrew and Aramaic-Hebrew scripts), Der Schaubrodts-Tisch an sich selbt ad. pag. 122, Gestalt der Cherubim auf dem Knaden-Stul, ad. pag. 14, M&uuml;nze der erster Purim ad. pag. 1071 (Seals with the Hebrew Tetragrammaton, with Latin text Dexter A Tua domine percussit inimicum, Vulgate translation for Psalms 117-16) ; Grund-riss des Feld-Lagers der kinder Israel (Ground scheme of the campsite of the Children of Israel, i.e. Ten Tribes) - pull-out table ; Des Salomonischen eigentlich so genannten Tempels von aufser (The Solomonic Temple, so-called the first Temple) ; Grundriss des inneren Vorhofes wie er zur Zeit Herodis gewesen (building-plan for the inner-court (&rsquo;Azarah) as it existed in Herod&rsquo;s plan) - pull-out table ; Das Eherne Meer (The Iron Sea - perhaps the groundwells of Solomon in Jerusalem) - extend-plate of bulls hoisting a tub of water, with bulls-head spigots flushing water ; das hohe Priestes in seinem Schmuck / ein seneiner Priester in seiner Kleidung (The High-Priest in his jewels / a working-Priest (i.e. a general Priest) in his clothes). Continued : Der G&ouml;tze Moloch wie ihme die Kinder zum Opfer in seine gluende Arme gegeben / Der G&ouml;tze Moloch mit 7 R&auml;umen oder Capellen (The Idol Moloch with the child for offering in its arms - The Idol Moloch with seven rooms or Chapels) - two woodcuts of the Moloch with a bull&rsquo;s head and an Egyptian priests body on a round three-step pedestal, with a burning pyre in its gut - first holding a child, second showing seven block-openings on it&rsquo;s chest) ; Unterschieditsche Hennungen wie die Priestes ... (manipulating the hands like the Priests) ; deine zesfel in hauptform des Denetzesfels (the Cube in central-form of the cube-Phylacteries). On the first forward of Henricus Muhlius D. (Heinrich Muhle) the top of the leaf is crowned with three letter &rsquo;yud&rsquo; in a triangle, with an eight-pointed star, and a horn; the leaf [1092] has the full Hebrew tetragrammaton. Frontispiece: Author&rsquo;s portrait in circular quarter-page woodcut, surrounded by titles. Underneath, an engraved quote : Lundius hic, per quam vivunt morte obruta dudum -- templa, sacerdotes, sacra Hierosolyma -- vivit et ipso, nova in Solyma Templum, atque Sacerdotes -- Immortali Agno Sacra Perrene facit. Joh. Albertuss Fabricius, D.S.S. Frontispiece signed : J.G. Mentzel s.c. (sculpta sit). Engravings : I.W. Michaels fecit. (fecitare). Das vierdte register: aller autorum, nebst ihren augezogenen schrifften p. [13]-[16] at end. Deutsch, Yaacov. Judaism in Christian eyes: ethnographic descriptions of Jews and Judaism in early modern Europe. Oxford: Oxford University Press, 2011, pp. 161-163. From the Harvard Art Museums&rsquo; collections Johann Lund, no. R8789, frontispiece. https://www.harvardartmuseums.org/art/247572 Bonomi, Carlo. The Cut and the Building of Psychoanalysis, Volume I : Sigmund Freud and Emma Eckstein. Florence: Taylor and Francis, 2015, Illustrations of Moloch, Moloch with Child, pp. 162.</p>" ;
    dc:publisher "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/b752ab25-1ee4-5c1d-8e14-e5f423d72577" ;
    dc:title "Die alten jüdischen heiligthümer" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-17T14:44:00.520537"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Die alten jüdischen heiligthümer" .

