    jl:hasAbstract "",
        "(chronogram לפרט צד’ק’ת’ ה ע’שה [תקעד]) seen in Friedberg, Beit 'Eked Sefarim, lamed 565:6 but a variant of Friedbergs. See The Bibliography of the Hebrew Book, record no. 000411399. Quoted there is the variants of the 1814 and 1815 printings of the Tanya in Y. Mondshine, (heb.) 'The Book of Tanya: Editions, Translations, and Commentaries (Kfar HaBad, Kahot, 1982)', pp. 61. This is the first of two variants printed in Shkloŭ after the death of Shneu'r Zalman of Liadi." ;
    dc:publisher "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/0d7c3f1b-1186-55b6-9f71-53c14c716a7f",
