    jl:hasAbstract "",
        "Masekhet Shabbat is bound together with another Masekhet. While the binding is the same as Masekhet Berakhot (vols. 1-2), printed in 1734 in Berlin/Frankfurt de Oder by Aaron ben Moshe Rofe, it is hard to detect when they were bound. But, they are part of the same set, printed between 1734 and 1739.",
        "Subtitle: [עם פירוש רשי ותוספות].<br />BHB note: אוצר 29 A.",
        "This is Bomberg's second printing of Shabbat." ;
