<http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/870af9c4-ab40-5915-aa6b-d0d26c11f93f> a gndo:Work ;
    gndo:associatedPlace "Amsterdam",
        "אמשטרדם" ;
    gndo:author "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/39e97a30-b547-5450-a5c7-d972187a3f85" ;
    gndo:dateOfPublication "1730" ;
    gndo:formerOwner "Baltimore Hebrew College",
        "Elhanan-Hennele b. Netanel of Mannheim",
        "Jewish Cultural Reconstruction",
        "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library",
        "Lemle Moses Klaus-Stifung Mannheim",
        "Mosheh b. Elhanan-Henelle ",
        "Städtische Schlossbücherei Mannheim" ;
    gndo:language "Hebrew" ;
    gndo:owner "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library" ;
    gndo:printer "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/536eac9a-2982-5889-9754-379c6d648654" ;
    jl:describedAt "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000118712&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "all notes by Chaim Meiselman:  notes    This is the first printing of the volume Yesod ha-Nikud, a treatise on Hebrew vowels and word-formation, with some limited discussion also on Hebraic etymology. According to the Haskamot, this volume seems to have made an impact in the Yeshivot in Germany at the time of the printing.      Haskamot of the rabbinic delegation of the Spanish-Portugese Community of Amsterdam, with David-Yisrael Athias and Yitshak-Hayyim ibn Dana Breto signing, 27 Sivan 1730; Moshe Frankfurt of the Ashkenazic Community of Amsterdam; Yehudah Möller of Bingen am Rhein, residing in Kleve, 8 Sivan 1730; Samuel Heilmann in Mannheim, signing 15 Elul 1727.      Title in architechture made from ornaments; some ornaments through the remainder of the title. Single text block on leaves.   references    Friedberg, Beit Eked Sefarim, Yod 764      Steinschneider, M., Cat. Libr. Hebr. Bodl., 6922 : 3      Vinograd, v. 2, p. 61 Amsterdam 1365" ;
    dc:title "Yesod ha-Niḳud" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-18T02:31:39.924618"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Yesod ha-Niḳud" .

