<http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/94b6936d-2b60-5fac-8c03-4442d968c41c> a gndo:Work ;
    gndo:associatedPlace "Lviv" ;
    gndo:author "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/858d9df4-e6ab-5840-b5ee-2450050d78e0" ;
    gndo:dateOfPublication "1796" ;
    gndo:formerOwner "Baltimore Hebrew College",
        "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library",
        "Rapaport?",
        "Russian State Library",
        "Yosef Yitzhak Schneerson (Sixth Lubavicher Rebbe)" ;
    gndo:language "Hebrew" ;
    gndo:owner "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library",
        "Russian State Library" ;
    jl:describedAt "https://search.worldcat.org/de/title/884509022" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "Not in BHB.  All notes by Chaim Meiselman:  notes    This is the first printing of the volume Ḳetsot ha-Ḥoshen by Aryeh-Löb ha-kohen Heller (Kalush 1745 - Stryj 1812). It is a celebrated text among the commentaries on the Shulhan ’Arukh Hoshen ha-Mishpat, renowned for sharp Pilpul and wide-ranging halakhic queries.      The addendum to the volume is the Ḳunṭros ha-Sefeḳot by Yehudah ha-Kohen Heller, the author’s brother.      Added editors to the volume: Yehudah-Löb Reiss of Buchach and Yitshak Frenkel of Lviv.      With a dedication to Francis II, Holy Roman Emperor on title in Hebrew: Taḥat memshelet adonenu ... ḳesar (i.e. Kaiser) romischer ungarin fihm galitsien ... Franz ha-sheni.      Printed with double-columns with bold-type and some maniculae.      Vol. 2 printed in 1795. zu Drucken erlaubt. Lemberg der 16ten Junne 1795.   references    Friedberg, Beit Eked Sefarim, Ḳuf no. 1004 : 1      Zedner, Cat. Heb. British Museum, p. 54" ;
    dc:title "Ketsot ha-Hoshen" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-17T16:31:42.735039"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ketsot ha-Hoshen" .

