    jl:describedAt "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000122016&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://search.worldcat.org/de/title/873037745" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "",
        "Latif printed two editions of this pamphlet; in an article in Kiryat Sefer (vol. IV, p. 226, no. 25) Yizhak Rivkind notes the resettings. Four short treatises on ceremonies to be observed at meal-times. A Constantinople edition—also undated—of the same text was printed around the same time (St 4525,17). One of only a few books from a mysterious and short-lived Hebrew press, Mantua's second. Rare (not in the major post-war auction sales)." ;
