    jl:hasAbstract "",
        "With reprinted haskamot of Gabriel Dielrioe, Emmanuel Hai Rikki, and Malahi b. Ya’akov ha-kohen; added haskamah for the second printing from Avraham Mordekhai b. Israel Halperin of Zolḳiew.      While the correspondence in the last section (and two pieces printed after the opening haskamot) are called a general term of Shu.t., they are on topics of kabbalah, faith, and philosophical essentials - different than standard Rabbinic responsa (containing Talmudic topics). -Chaim Meiselman   Title reads ’Amsterdam’ in large letters, but this is just a statement of the printers.      1st edition published in Amsterdam in 1736; this is 2nd edition." ;
    dc:contributor "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/19fdbb56-a498-5f0b-a781-7f9cadf65084",
