<http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/ad4a228e-9ab8-5521-a17a-29e8a84c7bf3> a gndo:Work ;
    gndo:associatedPlace "Amsterdam",
        "Fiorda",
        "אמשטרדם",
        "פיורדא" ;
    gndo:author "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/3170b733-45fc-5260-972c-a7ae3ab95c79",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/b4cd288f-ad6d-517f-816e-283006332fc6",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/c85c2cd3-ed88-5a99-934a-9fbeb2cac53e",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/e0045b7d-b19f-5d21-a2cc-c030c3c74135" ;
    gndo:dateOfPublication "1711",
        "1758" ;
    gndo:formerOwner "Baltimore Hebrew College",
        "Columbia University Libraries",
        "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library",
        "Kloyz Yasod",
        "Temple Emanu-el" ;
    gndo:language "Hebrew" ;
    gndo:owner "Columbia University Libraries",
        "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library" ;
    gndo:printer "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/76d61e7b-0759-54a5-a841-701896a11876",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/c9b3c84b-9f26-5119-88e5-76fa191b88bf" ;
    jl:describedAt "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000200833&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,002069855&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "",
        "All notes by Chaim Meiselman:   notes    Contents follow the text, followed by a poem written by Sabbetai b. Meir ha-kohen.      Added printers at colophon: Yissakhar-Ber of Minden-am-Weser, and Yosef b. Mosheh Segal from Hamburg.      A long title statement documents the publishing of this edition. Scholars from the Beth-Hamidrash of Fürth: Nathan-Nata b. Shemu’el, Nathan-Nata b. Löb, and Lima b. Naftali; according to the statement, these men toiled with Shelomoh Proops to perfect this edition of the Shulhan Arukh. These men are also heavily praised in the haskamot.      Haskamot on this edition: Tsvi-Hersch b. Ya’akov of the Ashkenazic community of Amsterdam, dated 2 Iyyar 1711; Solomon Ayyalon of the Spanish-Portugese community of Amsterdam, 23 Iyyar 1711; David Oppenheim of Prague, 9 Iyyar 1710; Naftali ha-kohen Katz of Frankfurt, 11 Iyyar 1710; Gavri’el b. Yehudah, Av-Beth-Din of Nicolsburg (Mikulov), 28 Adar 1711; Avraham of Metz, 21 Adar 1710; Ya’akov b. Meir Poppers (author of She’elot u-Teshuvot Shev Ya’akov) of Koblenz, 21 Adar 1710.      Layout in this edition: the center-block is the main text (Karo, Isserles); the gutter-edge text is David ha-levi’s Ṭurei zahav, often covering the complete folio; the margin-edge is Sabbetai b. Meir ha-Kohen’s Sifte Kohen. The outer margin text is Moses Rivkes’ Be’er ha-Golah.   references    Steinschneider, M. Cat. Libr. Hebr. Bodleiana, 5940 : 60 & 61",
        "Note by Chaim Meiselman:  Note  Printing scheme: Text of the code and general glosses in the center-top, flanked by Turei Zahav on the gutter-edge side and Sifte Kohen on the margin-edge side; margins covered by Be'er ha-Golah (Moses Rivkes).  General Note  Haskamot of this edition: Samuel Heilman of Metz, Friday 27 Sivan 1756; Yitshak-Zekyl Ötthausen of Pfersee (Augsburg; spelled פפערשא) 22 Kislev 1756; Aryeh-Lob Rapaport of Heissfeld-Würzburg, dated Thursday 19 Shvat 1758; Eliezer Katzenellenbogen of Haganau, dated 8 Tamuz 1756; Nathaniel Weill in Kahrlsruhe, dated 14 Sivan 1755. Introductions follow; first that of David HaLevi Segal (1586-1667) to his commentary Turei Zahav; Poem and introduction of Shabtai b. Meir ha-Kohen Katz (1621-1662) to his commentary Sifte Kohen; introduction by the printer; finally, acknowledgements and disclaimers also by the printer.  General Note  Engraved t.p. - depicting Moses and Aaron in an indealized architechtural structure." ;
    dc:contributor "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/372546e6-f767-5663-a4d1-486a99ee05fc",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/87f1f100-1e67-5d63-97cc-42f13d33ae46",
