<http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/ad85fc57-c6cc-5059-b932-3b789d7c399e> a gndo:Work ;
    gndo:associatedPlace "L'viv",
        "Lviv",
        "Lviv (Lemberg)" ;
    gndo:author "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/e58f2d40-9eb5-5bc1-900b-38573530b442" ;
    gndo:dateOfPublication "1795",
        "1858" ;
    gndo:formerOwner "Baltimore Hebrew College",
        "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library",
        "Russian State Library",
        "Yosef Yitzhak Schneerson (Sixth Lubavicher Rebbe)" ;
    gndo:language "Hebrew" ;
    gndo:owner "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library",
        "Russian State Library" ;
    gndo:printer "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/ec7bd892-a7ae-59e5-8b0c-41f445970751" ;
    jl:describedAt "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000181318&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000181319&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://search.worldcat.org/de/title/918486078" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "All notes by Chaim Meiselman:  notes    This work is associated with the Kabbalistic (Lurianic) work of Nathan Spira, also with the title of Megaleh Amukot, which is specifically focused on a portion in Deuteronomy. This edition was the first printing of the work ranging on the order of the Torah.      Edited, with a preface by Israel b. Zechariah Pineles of Levov; he is identified in the Haskamot as a descendant of Nathan Nata Spira.      Haskamot of Zvi-Hirsch Berlin-Loewenstamm (also known as Reverend Hart Lyon, former Chief Rabbi of England), signed in Berlin on 13 Tamuz 1795; Zvi-Hersch Rosenes of Levov, signing 25 Av 1795; Mosheh Zvi-Hersch Maizeles of Zolkiew, signing 19 Av 1795; Alexander (Szender) Margolioth of Sataniv, signing 4 Tamuz 1795; then an introduction by Ephraim Zalman Margolioth of Brody.      Title surrounded by quotations and lines of ornaments.      With a dedication in German (employing Hebrew charachters) on the title to Francis II, Holy Roman Emporer (1768-1835). Curiously, the subsequent line reads that the printing was finished on 16 January 1795 (dating the Anno Domini with Hebrew charachters).   references    Friedberg, Beit Eked Sefarim, mem 501 : 1 (second count)." ;
    dc:title "Megaleh amukot" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-17T18:01:10.859545"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Megaleh amukot" .

