    jl:hasAbstract "All notes by Chaim Meiselman:  The first section of this work is responsa following the order of Shulḥan ʻarukh Oraḥ ḥayim. The final section is composed of novellae following the Talmudic Orders of Nashim and Neziḳin.With an introduction by the author, with a running title of 'Haḳdamat Ben Levi'.Haskamot of Jacob Meshullam b. Mordekhai Ze'ev Orenstein of Lviv, signing 1 Kislev 1834; Jacob b. Jacob-Mosheh of Lissa (Leszno), signing 14 Tishrei 1831 in Stryi (weeks before his passing, also at Stryi); Moses Schreiber (Hatam Sofer) of Pressburg, i.e. Bratislava, signing in Frankfurt-am-Main; Eli'ezer of Miklosz (Liptovský Mikuláš, Slovakia), signing 23 Tevet 1828.Steinschneider, M., Cat. Libr. Hebr. Bodl.,4435 : 1Friedberg, C.D., Beit Eked Sefarim,beit 584" ;
    dc:title "She'elot u-Teshuvot (Aryeh Leib Horowitz)" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-17T22:19:28.488794"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "She'elot u-Teshuvot (Aryeh Leib Horowitz)" .

