        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000303933&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "<p>All notes by Chaim Meiselman: notes Text ends with the Akdamut Milin of Meir b. Isaac of Orleans (11th cent.), recited on the first day of Shavu&rsquo;ot. Imprint censorship statement in Polish, dated 6 May 1819 in Vilnius, F.N. Colanski. Rubricated elements (title element, printer&rsquo;s name, place of print) on title. Long secondary imprint information on the title, detailing the specifics of this edition. The order was written in the volume Shene Luḥot Habrit by Isaiah b. Abraham Horowitz (1555-1630), and is similar to many of the East-European imprints of this volume of the near-period (ex. Ostroha, 1827; Lemberg, 1837). With a title dedication to Nicholas I of Russia (1796-1855). Chronogram: בשנת ו.ה.ג.י.ת. .ב.ו. יו.מ.ם. .ו.ל.י.ל.ה. לפק. references Friedberg, Beit Eked Sefarim, tav 1816 : 22</p>" ;
    dc:publisher "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/ae1c2ce1-b8b9-5c22-93f3-0c2c7652988a",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/fab7152f-2100-5377-9596-b41532b70816" ;
    dc:title "Tikun lel Shavu`ot" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-18T01:36:54.269856"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Tikun lel Shavu`ot" .

