        "Yosef Yitzhak Schneerson (Sixth Lubavicher Rebbe)" ;
    gndo:language "Hebrew" ;
    gndo:owner "Joseph Meyerhoff Collection, Towson University Library",
        "Russian State Library" ;
    gndo:printer "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/9b7661c3-1154-5869-a5e9-4f4d9f90bf67",
        "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/e0f75b1b-43da-5670-89e4-e79a66beae78" ;
    jl:describedAt "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000180053&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000180060&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000181054&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000181069&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000200766&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://merhav.nli.org.il/primo-explore/search?query=any,contains,000315866&tab=default_tab&search_scope=Local&vid=NLI&lang=en_US&offset=0",
        "https://search.worldcat.org/de/title/233348506",
        "https://search.worldcat.org/de/title/696139327",
        "https://search.worldcat.org/de/title/794818201" ;
    jl:hasAbstract "",
        "All notes by Chaim Meiselman:  On the last leaf is a table of dates for the holidays and selected Torah readings, beginning from 1827 'until the end of the sixth milennia (ha-elef ha-shishi)', i.e. 3240 A.D. At the completion of the table, the words 'Ashre ha-meḥakeh', i.e. 'Special are those who [are] wait[ing]' (Daniel 12:12).Layout for this edition: The text (Joseph Karo and Moses Isserles) is at the center, surrounded by David ha-levi's Ture Zahav on the gutter-edge, and Avraham Abele's Magen Avraham on the margin-edge. The small text in the margin is headed by Moses Rivkes' Be'er ha-Golah at the top, and below that is Menahem-Mendel Aurbach's Ateret Zekenim; on the bottom of the page is Yehudah Ashkenazi's Be'er Hetiv.The volume begins with a note of copyright to the Slavuta printers, signed (in the presence of two witnesses) on 24 Adar II 1821, in the presence of Yosef b. Tsevi ha-kohen, the judge. Further Haskamot from rabbinical figures : Mordekhai Twersky ('The Maggid') of Chernobyl, signing in Berdichyv on 22 Sivan 1826; Hayyim b. Peretz hakohen of Pinsk, signing in Iziaslav on 5 Av 1825; Haim haKohen Rapaport of Ostroh, 18 Elul 1827; Mordekhai Margolioth of Brody, presiding over Sataniv, 15 Elul 1827; Yosef b. Meir of Starokostiantyniv, 5 Elul 1827; Yitshak-Eizek of Berdichyv, 28 Adar 1827; Efraim of Sudylkiv, 27 Elul 1827; finally, Yehuda-Leib and Eli'ezer, dayanim of Ostroh, 2 Elul 1827.Censor date 2 Feb. 1819 in Vilno (Vilnius) by F.N. Golanski, with the main-title heading the censorship statement - Mugine Yryc.",
        "The text layout of the volume follows the text (Karo's Shulhan Arukh and Isserles' ha-Mapah) at the top center in bold, and to the margin-edge is Moses Rivkes' Be'er ha-Golah. Moses Frankfurter's Be'er Hetiv is a wide column at the bottom." ;
    dc:publisher "http://data.judaicalink.org/data/footprints/c55a8b9a-112c-5f60-b796-a73c4c62b1e0" ;
    dc:title "Shulhan arukh. Orah Hayim" ;
    dcterms:created "2024-03-18T00:25:23.287192"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:prefLabel "Shulhan arukh. Orah Hayim" .

